## ASSUMPTIONS.

- “Intermediate” means the learner understands basic conversational interfaces and ordinary media production but does not know a particular implementation platform.
- No jurisdiction, deployment context, learner population, institutional policy, or technical stack was supplied.
- The previous proposal’s content and the authoring ensemble’s underlying reasons were not supplied. Only the refusal notice was available. Reproducing or comparing the previous content was therefore impossible. This retry uses an original, standards-led structure centered on system stages, recovery design, equivalent media, and evaluation.
- Generic terms such as speech recognition, captions, transcripts, keyboard interface, and audio description refer to techniques or media forms, not named tools or products.

## OMITTED.

- Product-specific implementation instructions, tool names, configuration keys, and platform settings were omitted because none were established by the supplied material.
- Numerical performance thresholds and test sample sizes were omitted because no supportable values were supplied.
- Legal compliance conclusions were omitted because the applicable jurisdiction and deployment context are UNKNOWN.
